subject: refactor(messages): extract shared messageFormats module + dedupe formatters

Research recommendation (refactor subagent): the page.js and export route
each defined their own prettyJson/buildCurl/extractText/buildMarkdown,
which could drift. Extracted a shared src/shared/messageFormats.js:

- prettyJson, buildCurl (with _truncated detection), extractText (with
  depth guard), buildMarkdown — used by both the page (client) and the
  export API route (server)
- Page keeps its RICHER local buildMarkdown (role-styled request + provider
  payload sections) but imports prettyJson/buildCurl/extractText from the
  shared module
- Export route now imports buildCurl/buildMarkdown from the shared module,
  deleting its local duplicates (net -90 lines)

Also fixes extractText infinite-recursion risk (depth cap at 10) flagged in
the audit (B6).

VERIFICATION: build passes; export route + page both compile against the
shared module.

Part of: Messages Page + Error Inbox plan (P1 refactor)

